  "description": "Here is a 5-line summary of the conversation:\n\n1. The task was to add a `view` property (`grid` | `column`) to kanban boards and split the UI into two separate view components.\n2. The existing column/drag-and-drop layout was extracted into a new **`KanbanColumnView.vue`** component, accepting `columns`, `filter`, and `lastUpdatedTaskId` as props and emitting events upward.\n3. A new **`KanbanGridView.vue`** component was created featuring a rich filter bar (text search, column, profile, mode, date, pinned toggle) and a responsive card grid with grouping support.\n4. **`Kanban.vue`** was updated to read the active view from `activeKanbanBoard.view` via a `currentView` computed property, and a `setView()` method persists the chosen view to the board store.\n5. A toggle button group was added to the toolbar in `Kanban.vue` allowing users to switch between the column and grid views seamlessly.",
